# Normalise line endings. Without this, editing from Windows/OneDrive and from
# a Linux toolchain flips CRLF<->LF on whole files and every diff is noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.m4a binary

# --- pcb/ : preserve bytes exactly -------------------------------------------
# KiCad and the fab exports are CRLF on disk, and release-hashes.json /
# package_a3.py record sha256 of those exact bytes. The eol=lf rule above would
# rewrite them on checkout and silently invalidate every recorded hash, so the
# whole tree opts out of normalisation. `-text` (not `binary`) keeps diffs
# readable -- schematic and layout changes still review as text.
pcb/** -text

# ...except things with no useful textual diff.
*.zip binary
*.ses binary
